.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH LINEAR 1 2000-1月 "export_profiles" "export_profiles"
.SH NAME
export_profiles \- Run the perturbation experiment for a set of genes and save the profiles as a csv file.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIexport_profiles(\fBmodel\fR as <generic> ElasticNet, 
\fBgenes\fR as any, 
\fBfile\fR as string, 
\fBmode\fR as string = "knockdown", 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Run the perturbation experiment for a set of genes and save the profiles as a csv file.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBmodel\fB \fR\- the perturbation engine that is created via \fBelastic_model\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgenes\fB \fR\- the target gene ids. 
.PP
.PP
\fBfile\fB \fR\- the output csv file, its folder will be created automatically. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmode\fB \fR\- \fBknockout\fR, \fBknockdown\fR (default) or \fBoverexpress\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
TRUE when the file has been written successfully
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
The first column is the gene id, the second column is the control (wildtype) profile,
 and the following columns are the mutant profiles of the given perturbations.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
linear
.SH FILES
.PP
TRNtoolkit.dll
.PP
